:level  L16
:name   Wet the Landing
:teach  the water jug — wet the cell your own fan is about to hit, and the trash lands as floor
:arm    on
:par    6
:traps  21
:solves 1
:solve  UruU!ll
:note   The fan is going to hit (3,2) whichever way you play it. Leave it dry and that cell becomes trash, a wall between you and the door; shove the jug up first and it becomes water, and the same fan fills it in as a bridge. Two moves cheaper than walking round, and the whole piece in one strike.
:grid
-----
-E-$-
-----
--j--
--@--
:end

:level  L17
:name   Both Ends
:teach  furniture — it spans cells, so both ends need room, and it is cheapest along its own length
:arm    on
:par    7
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  uurDR!lu
:note   Shove the couch sideways and the cell in front of the end you touched is empty — but the bag sits in front of its other end, and that refuses the whole shove. Pushed the way it lies it asks for one new cell instead of two, and that is the shove that frees the bag's launch cell.
:grid
-E---
-F$--
@F---
-----
:end

